    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39347" root="نجب" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَجَبٌ</span></b>  The <i>bark</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لِحَآء</span>) of trees: (S, K:) or the
<i>rind of the roots</i> thereof: or <i>of what is hard</i>
thereof. (K.) The soft peel of branches is not
thus called; nor is the rind of roots called <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قِشْر</span>,
but <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نجب</span>: n. un. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَجَبَةٌ</span>. (TA.)

